<p>On the basis of exchange rates on 1 - 6 August 1997, the average UK RMG is greater than +5 per cent, at 9.458 per cent. It is, therefore currently forecast to enter its fifth and final confirmation period on 11 August. If it remains above +5 per cent for these two remaining 10-day confirmation periods, the UK green rate faces revaluation on 21 August 1997. All currencies with negative RMGs for this period will devalue on 11 August by reducing their gaps to zero. Hence, further devaluations are currently forecast for the Danish, Spanish and Portuguese green rates. During confirmation periods the 3-day (6 per cent) rule is suspended.</p>
